MojoProof sweep corpus: notice for the files in tests/sweep/

The files named *.nvptx.ll here are LLVM IR that the Mojo compiler (1.3.0.dev2026112705) wrote
for the GPU kernels of the Mojo test sources listed below (`mojo build --emit llvm
--target-accelerator <arch>`), kept by scripts/safe_sweep.py (docs/proofs/safe.md): of each
(kernel library function, test file) pair, the smallest per-kernel file. Each file's row in
MANIFEST.tsv (this directory's own manifest, which scripts/corpus.py reads with
`--root tests/sweep`) records its Mojo version, its flags, its source and the source's sha256,
and the library file that defines the kernel's function. The IR is compiled from those sources
and from the library code they import.

The sources come from the Modular repository, https://github.com/modular/modular, at commit
483e1348c8adab60d67d2857272cefc706d7e217 (483e1348). Their headers read:

    Copyright (c) 2026, Modular Inc. All rights reserved.

    Licensed under the Apache License v2.0 with LLVM Exceptions:
    https://llvm.org/LICENSE.txt

The license text is in LICENSE-APACHE-LLVM, next to this file. The library code that these
kernels import comes from the same commit: the Mojo standard library and the MAX kernel library
(max/kernels/src), under the same license.

